My husband Justin and I
produced a documentary

00:07:27.701 --> 00:07:30.334
about Broadway
returning after COVID.

00:07:30.334 --> 00:07:31.801
And it's -- We just found out

00:07:31.801 --> 00:07:33.434
we're gonna be premiering
at the Tribeca Film Festival.

00:07:33.434 --> 00:07:34.534
-Hey!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:34.534 --> 00:07:38.000
-Perfect.
-Yeah.

00:07:38.000 --> 00:07:39.534
It's called "Broadway Rising."

00:07:39.534 --> 00:07:40.834
-"Broadway Rising."
-Yeah.

00:07:40.834 --> 00:07:42.901
-I mean, this city
is the greatest city on Earth.

00:07:42.901 --> 00:07:45.000
I mean, we're lucky enough
to have Broadway.

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:47.934
You know, and as a show,
we have Broadway even here

00:07:47.934 --> 00:07:50.234
but on our show as a guest.

00:07:50.234 --> 00:07:51.968
And man, they got hit, you know.

00:07:51.968 --> 00:07:53.067
-They got hit so hard.

00:07:53.067 --> 00:07:54.634
And so many people
lost their jobs.

00:07:54.634 --> 00:07:56.100
Not just the actors
and the directors

00:07:56.100 --> 00:07:57.734
and producers,
but like, all the restaurants

00:07:57.734 --> 00:07:59.400
in Times Square,
and, like, the dry cleaners

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:01.000
who clean the costumes
up in the Bronx.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:02.467
And so our documentary
really celebrates

00:08:02.467 --> 00:08:04.334
that entire community.

00:08:04.334 --> 00:08:06.467
So it's a really special film.
-Jesse Tyler Ferguson,

00:08:06.467 --> 00:08:08.367
you're a good man.
Thank you for doing this.

00:08:08.367 --> 00:08:10.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
Congrats on the play.

00:08:10.267 --> 00:08:13.100
Go see "Take Me Out"
on Broadway,

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:14.300
now through June 11th.

